Subject: media: meson: vdec: add Meson8m2 H.264 decoding

VDEC_1 of the S812 runs the Meson8 H.264 microcode, which speaks the same
mailbox protocol as the GXBB one. Differences handled here:

- AO power registers through the Meson8 syscon (&pmu, AO + 0xe0), and only
  the VDEC_1 isolation bits are touched;
- the VDEC_1 clock is not set by the driver, DT assigns fclk_div4
  (637.5 MHz): a rate request could move vdec_1_sel to an audio MPLL;
- H.264 start as in the vendor vh264_prot_init(): VLD reset, PSCALE off,
  no SEI buffer (AV_SCRATCH_I/J), no AV_SCRATCH_F bit 7; commands 4 and 5
  (slice groups) are acked quietly;
- the AMRISC cores are reset before MPSR = 1, as in the vendor amvdec_start();
- firmware DMA is polled with a 100 ms timeout instead of 1000 reads;
- Meson8 canvases have no known endianness control, so the canvases are set
  without a swap and the frames come out as the decoder writes them. Two
  test parameters pass endianness bits anyway: meson_vdec.meson8_endian and
  meson_canvas.meson8_endian;
- meson_canvas_config() errors are no longer ignored for NV12M, and a failed
  canvas setup aborts the H.264 session;
- generic fix: if the CAPTURE queue is set up between the firmware's
  "parameters" interrupt and amvdec_src_change(), changed_format is cleared
  and STREAMON never resumes the decoder (the firmware waits forever). The
  CAPTURE STREAMON now also resumes when the allocated buffers fit the
  stream (same size, enough buffers). Hit with ffmpeg h264_v4l2m2m;
- generic fix: a new session claims the core with cmpxchg instead of a
  check and a later assignment. Two sessions starting at once both powered
  the decoder on; the first to stop powered it off under the other, whose
  next DOS register access hung the bus (hard lockup with two players);
- CAPTURE buffers (MMAP) are allocated cacheable (non_coherent_mem):
  copying a frame out of uncached memory took ffmpeg 28 ms per 720p
  frame. vb2 syncs the cache at QBUF/DQBUF. CREATE_BUFS without the
  non-coherent flag on such a queue is refused by vb2.

Firmware: meson/vdec/meson8_h264.bin, built by vdec/make-meson8-h264-fw.py
from the vendor 3.10 headers.

